@startuml skill_catalog
title Skill Command Catalog Resolution
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@c1311f69 mate-campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/matecampusclaw/codingagent/runtime/PreparedAgentRuntime.java:57-95
' Source evidence: pi-mono@4af9d21d packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts:754-765
' Observed behavior: both runtimes expose direct bound Skill name indexes.
' Target design: every bound Skill is user-invocable under the skill: namespace.

participant SkillCommandSource as Source
participant AgentRuntimeManager as Runtime
participant PreparedAgentRuntime as Snapshot

Source -> Runtime : prepareCached(agentId)
Runtime --> Source : latest complete Agent version
Source -> Snapshot : skills()
Snapshot --> Source : bound Skill metadata
Source -> Source : map validated 1..64 names to skill: namespace
@enduml

@startuml skill_acceptance
title Atomic Skill Command Acceptance
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@c1311f69 mate-campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/matecampusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java:81-112,275-293,425-433
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@c1311f69 mate-campusclaw/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeSessionMapper.xml:100-130
' Observed behavior: Agent snapshots are validated and published under an Agent-scoped lock.
' Target design: Skill content and Session acceptance commit as one replay-safe transaction.

participant SkillCommandHandler as Handler
participant AgentSkillSnapshotService as SnapshotService
participant AgentRuntimeManager as Runtime
database t_sessions as Sessions
database t_session_entries as Entries
database t_session_records as Records

Handler -> SnapshotService : snapshotLatestBoundSkill(agentId, name)
SnapshotService -> Runtime : read latest complete version under Agent lock
Runtime --> SnapshotService : metadata and full SKILL.md
SnapshotService --> Handler : immutable Skill snapshot
Handler -> Sessions : lock and require idle
Handler -> Entries : append active user.message with commandId
Handler -> Records : append private skill.snapshot
Handler -> Entries : append command.started sidecar
Handler -> Sessions : state=running, active leaf=user.message
note over Sessions,Records : One acceptance transaction
@enduml

@startuml skill_trust_layers
title Skill and User Input Trust Layers
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence: pi-mono@4af9d21d packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts:1315-1343
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@c1311f69 mate-campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/matecampusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/agent/RuntimeAgentPromptLoader.java:44-72
' Observed behavior: current implementations concatenate or format Skill content for model use.
' Security hardening: Skill instructions, user arguments, and attachments remain separate typed layers.

rectangle "Trusted Skill instruction layer" as Trusted
rectangle "User input layer\narguments" as User
rectangle "User attachment layer\nfileIds" as Files
rectangle "Model request assembler" as Assembler

Trusted --> Assembler : exact invocation snapshot
User --> Assembler : untrusted user content
Files --> Assembler : ordinary attachment semantics

note bottom of Assembler
Never concatenate all layers into one untyped text value.
disable-model-invocation affects automatic discovery only.
end note
@enduml

@startuml skill_replay
title Skill Replay After Agent Refresh
skinparam shadowing false

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@c1311f69 mate-campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/matecampusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java:131-153,366-380
' Observed behavior: managed Agent refresh atomically replaces the published directory.
' Target design: replay reads the invocation-local snapshot rather than the current directory.

database t_session_records as Records
participant SessionReplayService as Replay
participant ModelRequestAssembler as Assembler
collections "Current Agent files\nnew version or deleted Skill" as Current

Replay -> Records : load skill.snapshot by commandId
Records --> Replay : exact metadata and full content
Replay -> Assembler : trusted Skill layer
Replay -> Assembler : historical user arguments and attachments
Current -[#gray,dashed]-> Replay : not consulted
@enduml

@startuml skill_name_validation
title Target Strict Skill Name Validation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@0300541f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/skill/SkillNamePatterns.java:15-49
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@0300541f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/skill/SkillLoader.java:138-150
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@0300541f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/service/command/SkillCommandSource.java resolved
' Source evidence: pi-mono@4af9d21d packages/coding-agent/src/core/skills.ts loadSkillFromFile:320-344
' Observed behavior: Java loading uses LEGACY while command discovery uses STRICT; pi warns but still loads invalid names.
' Target-only design: all consumers use one strict Skill-domain rule; remove LEGACY loading.
' Design reason: invalid names must not enter loaded Skills, model discovery, command catalogs, or execution.
' Product constraint and security hardening: invalid existing names require correction before loading.

component "SkillLoader\nload-time rejection" as Loader
component "SkillCommandSource\ncommand discovery" as Discovery
component "Skill command execution\nvalidate before acceptance" as Execution
component "SkillNamePatterns\nSkill domain\nOne regex, Pattern, and length limit" as Rules

Loader --> Rules : shared strict rule
Discovery --> Rules : shared strict rule
Execution --> Rules : shared strict rule

note bottom of Rules
^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$
Length: 1..64 characters, checked separately.
No legacy rule or automatic name repair.
end note

note bottom of Loader
Require a string name in SKILL.md.
Require exact folder-name equality.
Invalid files never enter the loaded collection.
end note
@enduml
